          "comment": "Unplaced on both runs since reappearance win but this 3yo could still have more to offer",
          "spotlight": "Won on handicap and seasonal debut at Doncaster (5f, good to firm) in April; unable to kick on from that the next twice but hasn't run badly and this 3yo could still have more to offer; a tongue-tie goes on.",
          "medical": [],
          "quotes": [],
          "stable_tour": [
            {
              "horse": "Dothan",
              "horse_id": "6442163",
              "quote": "He won well on his first start of the year at Doncaster and has possibly been a touch disappointing since. Hamilton next time was a complicated track for a horse who doesn't have the best of actions, and then he ran over five furlongs at York and may need to step up to six furlongs on a Flat track. There's a race at Ayr coming up that I have in the back of my mind for him. 02-07-25"
            }
          ],
