          "comment": "Won at Ballinrobe in May, beaten at Royal Ascot latest, top rated and obvious chance",
          "spotlight": "Off the mark over hurdles on second start for this yard at Ballinrobe (16.5f, good) in May; smart form on the Flat for Andrew Balding but came up short back on the level in a hot Royal Ascot handicap three weeks ago; top-rated here at 128; obvious chance on ground that will suit.",
          "medical": [],
          "quotes": [
            {
              "date": "2024-07-12",
              "horse": "Fairbanks",
              "horse_id": "4566610",
              "race": "bet365 Trophy (Heritage Handicap)",
              "race_id": "869449",
              "course": "Newmarket (July)",
              "course_id": "crs_4524",
              "distance_f": "14",
              "distance_y": "3080",
              "quote": "With the blinkers on I wanted to ride Fairbanks further forward than I did, but he only jumped fairly so I didn't want to rush him up. It was a muddling tempo and he over raced around the bend, but he relaxed when I stopped fighting him. I didn't want him to be crowded with the blinkers on, so I sent him on a good way out and he was going to take a lot of beating from there. He could creep into the Ebor off his rating, but there is also a valuable consolation race too if Andrew [Balding, trainer] wants to go that route - Oisin Murphy, jockey."
            }
          ],
